{% tool-context
   title="Cache Simulator"
   question="Can this cache absorb real demand without hiding stale data or overwhelming the origin?"
   definition="A cache is a traffic-shaping layer. Demand shape, useful capacity, eviction, expiration, and refill behavior decide which requests stay on the fast path and which become origin work."
   inputs="Choose a workload, tune capacity, TTL, cache levels, and eviction policy, then inject a pressure scenario."
   outcome="Trace requests through cache and origin, compare load with the origin envelope, and inspect latency, duplicate fills, churn, and stale-response risk."
   experiment="Establish a healthy baseline, challenge it with hot-key skew, a miss storm, eviction churn, a slow origin, or stale-content risk, then enable each protection separately." /%}

